WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:05.529
As if Batman didn't have enough problems,
he's now facing accusations of thievery.

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:09.680
Since camera test footage of star Robert Pattinson
suited up for writer-director Matt Reeves'

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:13.950
The Batman was made public last week, some
fans have been taking to social media to pan

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.160
the new getup.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.250
It's not DC die-hards that are doing most
of the dissing, though.

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:22.740
It's Marvel fans, who seem to think that Battinson's
mask bears a little too much of a resemblance

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.680
to that worn by the Devil of Hell's Kitchen
in the Netflix series Daredevil.

00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:30.860
It doesn't help that the footage was absolutely
bathed in a candy apple red glow, which has

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.059
the effect of making the Dark Knight's suit
look as if it's been dyed Daredevil Red, and

00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:37.999
is also reminiscent of the Netflix series'
opening credits.

00:00:37.999 --> 00:00:42.579
Of course, the camera test footage didn't
give us a head-to-toe gander at the new Batsuit.

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:45.870
It mostly lingered on the chest piece, along
with the mask and cowl.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:49.920
It never does show us Bruce Wayne's Bat-ears,
which are typically set much further back

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.710
from the forehead than Daredevil's trademark
horns.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:56.629
So the similarity between the new Batsuit
and Daredevil's duds might not be quite so

00:00:56.629 --> 00:00:59.769
pronounced once we get a full-color, top-to-bottom
peek.

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:03.510
It's tough to argue, though, that the mask
Battinson is sporting with its shaped brow,

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:07.200
nose guard, and opening for the mouth and
chin that's cut nearly all the way back to

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.759
the temple doesn't look pretty Daredevil-esque.

00:01:09.759 --> 00:01:14.030
A strong contingent of Marvel fans came out
on Twitter to jeer at the new Batsuit pretty

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.859
much immediately after the test footage was
released.

00:01:16.859 --> 00:01:21.060
More than a few fans just angrily pointed
out the resemblance, like this user, who tweeted,

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.579
"I mean did they even try?"

00:01:23.579 --> 00:01:28.659
"These questions are vital ones."

00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:32.469
While others at least had a sense of humor
about the whole thing, like this user, who

00:01:32.469 --> 00:01:33.469
tweeted,

00:01:33.469 --> 00:01:36.310
"If Daredevil could see The Batman right now
he would be pissed."

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:40.420
As always, though, there were a few voices
of reason amid the chorus of boos.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:44.729
Deciding to go ahead and address every criticism
thus far leveled at Pattinson's Caped Crusader,

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:45.729
one user wrote,

00:01:45.729 --> 00:01:48.149
"Dear people still upset about the new Batman.

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:49.979
The suit and cowl is fine.

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:53.600
Yes that [looked] like Daredevil, it's not
just cause he's in red light.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.920
It's the shape of the cowl.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.460
Robert Pattinson has other roles aside from
Twilight.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:58.460
Watch The Lighthouse.

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.840
He doesn't need to be buff."

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:03.829
We've been saying ever since the casting was
announced that Pattinson is a criminally underrated

00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:07.119
actor who is going to make an absolutely fantastic
Batman.

00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:08.119
Need proof?

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:12.970
First, there's the 2017 crime drama Good Time,
which stars Pattinson as a bank robber desperately

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:16.300
trying to gather funds to get his simple-minded
brother out of prison.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.810
The flick was directed by the Safdie brothers,
who turned in one of the sharpest thrillers

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:23.190
in recent memory with last year's Uncut Gems.

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:26.910
Pattinson's performance in Good Time has been
hailed by critics as both brilliant, and about

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:30.000
as far from Edward Cullen as you can get.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.230
"As if you could outrun me!"

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:39.220
Next, we direct you to 2018's High Life, a
sci-fi/drama from acclaimed French director

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.650
Claire Denis.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:45.040
Pattinson stars as a condemned prisoner aboard
a deep-space mission bound for a black hole,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:50.180
and the movie's crazy, non-linear narrative
is absolutely anchored by his committed performance.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:54.120
Speaking of committed performances, you'd
also do well to follow the advice of the Twitterer

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.700
above and watch The Lighthouse, in which Pattinson
totally holds his own in what is essentially

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:02.250
a two-man acting showcase opposite the great
Willem Dafoe.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.250
"Easy!"

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:06.900
"Quit your flailing, lad!"

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.760
"I ain't!"

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:09.760
"Y'ar!"

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:13.450
All of the above movies are far from your
typical Hollywood fare, and they all demonstrate

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:17.500
that Pattinson is an actor of impressive range
who is more than capable of delivering an

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.800
interesting new take on Bruce Wayne.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:23.840
As for that Daredevil-y cowl... let's just
reserve judgment until we see some actual,

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.610
non-test footage, shall we?

